senses.gloss:
अभ्यय अभ्य्-अय, अस्, m. (fr. अभि-इ, see
अभी), going near, approaching, arriving; entering;
setting (of the sun).

अभ्य्-अञ्जन, अम्, n. smearing the body with oil,
inunction; oil; applying collyrium to the eyelashes;
ornament; embellishment.

अभ्यती अभ्य्-अती (अभि-अति-इ), cl. 2. P. अभ्य्-
अत्य्-एति, -तुम्, to go past, glide away; to pass over;
to get through.

अभ्यर्ष् अभ्य्-अर्ष् (अभि-अर्ष्), cl. 1. P. -अर्-
षति, -षितुम्, to flow near, to run near (with acc.);
to cause to flow near.

अभ्य्-असन, अम्, n. concentrating of the faculties
of the mind in one direction; practice, exercise;
repetition, study.

अभ्य्-आगम, अस्, m. or अभ्य्-आगमन, अम्, n.
approaching, arrival, visit, visitation; neighbourhood;
arriving at or enjoying a result; rising, getting up;
war, battle; encountering, striking, killing; enmity.

अभ्युपपद् अभ्य्-उप-पद् (अभि-उप˚), cl. 4. A.
-पद्यते, -पत्तुम्, to approach in order to help;
to deliver; to honour, to comfort; to ask for help;
to furnish with.

अभ्यृछ् अभ्य्-ऋछ् (अभि-ऋछ्), cl. 6. P.
-ऋच्छति, -छितुम्, to come to, to visit or afflict with;
to strive against, to strive to overpower.
